    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "Every selection has evidence in its own captured worked solution. Completing the square gives (y+6)^2-3, (x-5)^2+1, and (x-11)^2-4; expanding verifies the original expressions. For x^2+6x+14, 2p=6 and q=14-p^2=5. For y^2-10y+30, 2p=-10 and q=30-p^2=5. The six reciprocal graphs use vertical factors 5, 3/2, -3/4, -1/4, 1/2, and 3/4, with horizontal shifts left 1 and right 1 in the last two cases. Each selected image path exactly matches its question's final worked-solution image; image pixels were not supplied, so their visual accuracy cannot be independently checked. For q-113482, the solution reports b=3, k=0.5, and point (1,1.5), yielding a=(1.5-0.5)(1-3)=-2 and sum 1.5; the original graph is likewise unavailable for independent visual verification. The point transformations give (3,-2), (a+2,b+3), (4,1), and (3,-2), respectively: f(3)=1 gives -1-1=-2; substituting x=a+2 gives 2^a+3=b+3; 4f(4)=8 gives -f(4)+3=1; and f(3)-2=2 gives -f(3)+2=-2. No mathematical disagreement with the captured solutions was found. No previous submission or grade was supplied.",
